    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83b1f1f3_2369e8fc",
        "filename": "board/cr50/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 245,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-17T19:22:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I stopped enabling the wake pin in gpio.inc, so we don\u0027t need to disable it anywhere.\n\nThe interrupt on GPIO_SYS_RST_L_IN is always enabled. We just use the plt_rst_l signal for GPIO_SYS_RST_L_IN on reef boards and sys_rst as the signal on gru boards.",
      "parentUuid": "83b1f1f3_b4a3793e",
      "revId": "5aa418439e626494a5c4dd23d64845e8a6b04e6e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83b1f1f3_c3282cb6",
        "filename": "board/cr50/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 245,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-17T19:22:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need to disable the GPIO_SYS_RST_L_IN interrupt because we just switch the pad that that gpio is connected to based on the board. Gru will use the sys_rst_l signal and Reef uses the plt_rst_l signal.\n\nShould that gpio be renamed?",
      "parentUuid": "83b1f1f3_b4a3793e",
      "revId": "5aa418439e626494a5c4dd23d64845e8a6b04e6e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
